---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/site/Footer.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  loader={false}
  image="/og/terms.png"
  title={`Terms of Service — ${siteConfig.shortName}`}
  description={`Terms of Service for ${siteConfig.shortName}, the AI video editing Android app by ${siteConfig.companyLegalName}. Covers the service, accounts, your content, acceptable use, and contact details.`}
>
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="wrap doc-wrap">
      <!-- Back Link -->
      <div class="doc-back">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="label"
        >
          <svg
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2.5"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M19 12H5"></path>
            <path d="M12 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
          </svg>
          Back to Zera Studio
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Header -->
      <header class="doc-head">
        <span class="doc-eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1 class="d doc-h1">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <div class="doc-meta label">
          <span>Effective Date: October 14, 2026</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Applies to: {siteConfig.shortName} for Android</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Content -->
      <article class="doc-body">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Agreement to These Terms</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service ("Terms") apply to your use of {siteConfig.shortName}, the AI video editing Android application provided by {siteConfig.companyLegalName} ("Zera AI," "we," "our," or "us"), together with this website.
          </p>
          <p>
            By installing or using {siteConfig.shortName}, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the app.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. What Zera Studio Is</h2>
          <p>
            {siteConfig.shortName} is an AI-powered video editing application for Android. Its AI features add B-roll, motion graphics, zooms and captions to a talking video, or edit your clips in the style of a reference video. Every AI edit opens in a manual editor, where you can change it, preview it and export it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The AI editing functionality runs in the Android application. Our website is an informational company and product website and does not provide video editing in the browser.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Ongoing Development</h2>
          <p>
            {siteConfig.shortName} is publicly available and usable today, and it is <strong>under active development</strong>. Features may be added, changed, or removed as the product evolves, and you may encounter errors or interruptions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Price, Credits and Plans</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Free to download.</strong> Installing the app, the manual editor, effects and export are free.</li>
            <li><strong>Credits.</strong> AI features use credits. The number of credits a feature uses is shown in the app before you start it. If a run fails, the credits it used are returned.</li>
            <li><strong>Welcome credits.</strong> New accounts receive free welcome credits once per phone, on a phone that Google Play can verify. We may limit or withdraw free credits that are claimed through misuse, such as repeated accounts on one device.</li>
            <li><strong>Plans.</strong> Paid plans are monthly subscriptions sold and billed through Google Play. A plan adds its credits at the start of each billing period; unused plan credits do not carry over to the next period. Plans renew automatically until you cancel in Google Play, and cancelling keeps the plan until the end of the period already paid for.</li>
            <li><strong>Expiry.</strong> Welcome credits do not expire. Plan credits expire at the end of the billing period they were added for, as described under Plans.</li>
            <li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Payments are handled by Google Play and refunds follow Google Play's refund policies. If a payment is refunded or reversed, the credits it added are removed.</li>
            <li><strong>No cash value.</strong> Credits are not money, cannot be transferred or exchanged for cash, and are tied to your account.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Eligibility</h2>
          <p>
            {siteConfig.shortName} is not intended for children under 13 years of age, or under 16 where a higher minimum age is required by local law. By using the app you confirm that you meet the applicable minimum age.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Your Account</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>You are responsible for the accuracy of the account details you provide.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for keeping your login credentials secure.</li>
            <li>You may delete your account at any time. See our <a href="/account-deletion">Account Deletion Policy</a> for in-app and email options.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Your Content</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>You keep ownership.</strong> You retain all rights you already hold in the video clips, audio, images, and text you add to the app. We do not claim ownership of your content.</li>
            <li><strong>Limited processing permission.</strong> You grant us permission to process your content only as needed to provide the editing service to you — for example, uploading, analyzing, assembling, rendering, and returning your edited video.</li>
            <li><strong>Your responsibility.</strong> You confirm that you hold the necessary rights to the content you upload, including any music, footage, or images owned by someone else.</li>
            <li><strong>No monetization of your media.</strong> As stated in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, we do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information or private video media.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to use {siteConfig.shortName} to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Upload or generate content that is unlawful, or that infringes the intellectual property or privacy rights of others.</li>
            <li>Upload content involving the sexual exploitation or abuse of minors, or content that incites violence against others.</li>
            <li>Upload, create or edit sexually explicit or intimate images or videos of any real person without their consent, including AI-generated, "deepfake", "undress" or face-swapped content (non-consensual intimate imagery). {siteConfig.shortName} does not offer any feature for making such content, and we remove it and close the accounts involved.</li>
            <li>Impersonate a real person or make a video that falsely shows a real person saying or doing something, in order to deceive, harass or defraud.</li>
            <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, probe, or gain unauthorized access to the app, our accounts, or our processing infrastructure.</li>
            <li>Attempt to reverse engineer or extract the app's source code or models, except where such a restriction is prohibited by applicable law.</li>
            <li>Resell, redistribute, or provide the service to third parties as your own service.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Distribution and Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>
            {siteConfig.shortName} is distributed through Google Play, and your installation and use of the app is also subject to Google Play's own terms. As described in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, we use cloud infrastructure and machine learning processing services to deliver editing functionality.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Service Availability</h2>
          <p>
            Because {siteConfig.shortName} is under continuous development, we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue all or part of the service, including during maintenance or as the product develops.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, {siteConfig.shortName} is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. Automated editing results depend on the footage and reference material you provide, and we do not guarantee that a generated edit will meet a specific creative expectation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Zera AI will not be liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential losses arising from your use of {siteConfig.shortName}, including loss of data or lost project work. Nothing in these Terms excludes any liability that cannot be excluded under applicable law.
          </p>
          <p>
            We recommend keeping your own copies of any original footage that matters to you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Suspension and Termination</h2>
          <p>
            You may stop using {siteConfig.shortName} at any time and may delete your account as described in our <a href="/account-deletion">Account Deletion Policy</a>. We may suspend or terminate access where it is necessary to address a breach of these Terms, protect other users, or comply with a legal obligation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our handling of your data is described in the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of your use of {siteConfig.shortName}.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>15. Changes to These Terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these Terms as the product develops. Any revised version will be published on this page with an updated Effective Date. Continuing to use {siteConfig.shortName} after an update means you accept the revised Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="doc-end">
          <h2>16. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about these Terms, contact:
          </p>
          <div class="doc-card">
            <p class="doc-strong">{siteConfig.companyLegalName}</p>
            <p>Website: <a href={siteConfig.url}>{siteConfig.domain}</a></p>
            <p>Support: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a></p>
            <p>General contact: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</SiteLayout>
